{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "הן לה' אלהיך", :translit "hen laHashem elokecha", :gloss "Behold, to YHWH your Elohim"} {:he "שבה\"א נברא העולם", :translit "sheba'heh nivra ha'olam", :gloss "that with heh the world was created"} {:he "ה' חומשי תורה", :translit "heh chumshei Torah", :gloss "heh, five books of Torah"} {:he "לא ירדה שכינה למטה מעשרה", :translit "lo yardah shekhinah lematah me'asarah", :gloss "the Shekhinah did not descend below ten"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Verse begins and ends with letter heh"} {:kind :other, :note "Ten words in the verse correspond to ten degrees of divine descent"}], :frame {:text "The tradition that the world was created with the letter heh is stated in Menachot 29b, where Rava derives it from the verse \"הִנֵּה אֵל כְּבִירְיָתִי יָשַׁרְתִּי לְךָ\" (Isaiah 26:12), reading it as \"with heh these are created.\" That the Shekhinah does not descend below ten is stated in Sukkah 5a, derived from Isaiah 6:13 and other verses, and applied to a minyan of ten men in Berakhot 21b and Megillah 23b.", :sources ["Menachot 29b" "Sukkah 5a" "Berakhot 21b" "Megillah 23b" "Isaiah 26:12" "Isaiah 6:13"]}} {:quotes [{:he "הארץ וכל אשר בה", :translit "ha'aretz vechol asher bah", :gloss "the earth and all that is in it"} {:he "רק באבותיך", :translit "rak ba'avotecha", :gloss "only in your fathers"} {:he "שהארץ וכל אשר בה לא נבראה אלא בזכות האבות", :translit "sheha'aretz vechol asher bah lo nivra'ah ela bizechut ha'avot", :gloss "that the earth and all that is in it was not created except in the merit of the patriarchs"} {:he "רק באבותיך מיעוט הוא שגם עליהם יש דין", :translit "rak ba'avotecha mi'ut hu shegam aleihem yesh din", :gloss "only in your fathers is a limitation that even upon them there is judgment"} {:he "במה אדע", :translit "bemah eda", :gloss "how shall I know"} {:he "יצחק אהב את עשו", :translit "yitzchak ahav et esav", :gloss "Isaac loved Esau"} {:he "נסתרה דרכי מה'", :translit "nistarah derachi meHashem", :gloss "my way is hidden from YHWH"} {:he "ומלתם", :translit "umaltem", :gloss "and you shall circumcise"} {:he "תמולו ערלת הלב", :translit "temulu orlat halev", :gloss "you shall circumcise the foreskin of the heart"} {:he "כמו שעשו האבות", :translit "kemo she'asu ha'avot", :gloss "just as the patriarchs did"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition of הארץ וכל אשר בה with רק באבותיך teaches the earth was created in the merit of the patriarchs"} {:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition of רק באבותיך with ומלתם teaches circumcision of the heart as the patriarchs did"}], :frame {:text "The phrase במה אדע appears in Genesis 15:8, where Abraham asks how he shall know the land will be his. That Isaac loved Esau is stated in Genesis 25:28. Jacob saying נסתרה דרכי מה appears in Isaiah 40:27, understood by the midrash as applied to Jacob. The command ומלתם ערלת לבבכם appears in Deuteronomy 10:16.", :sources ["Genesis 15:8" "Genesis 25:28" "Isaiah 40:27" "Deuteronomy 10:16"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Verse begins and ends with letter heh", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Ten words in the verse correspond to ten degrees of divine descent", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition of הארץ וכל אשר בה with רק באבותיך teaches the earth was created in the merit of the patriarchs", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition of רק באבותיך with ומלתם teaches circumcision of the heart as the patriarchs did", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:35:53.676541280Z", :model "glm-5.2"}